{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719248666","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176#issuecomment-6719248666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176","id":6719248666,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkH-ZGg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?u=4a54630ef210e4f76a452eea65cda1b56370734c&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:26:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:26:00Z","author_association":"MEMBER","body":"The final integration dependency scan confirms that the proposed generic `Peptone.yaml` identity correction must be coupled to its component consumers. The frozen baseline has 19 incoming `MICRO:0000178` component claims; the proposed W02 MRSsi base contributes one additional claim. These are 20 distinct claims, not 20 approved target migrations.\n\nThe source-specific disposition is:\n\n- Eight generic-reference migration candidates: `Glucose_Peptone-yeast_Extract[1]`, `Marine_agar_2216[0]`, `PYGS[0]`, `Peptone-yeast_Extract-glucose[0]`, `Peptone_Beef_Extract_Yeast_Extract[0]`, `Peptone_Yeast_Extract[0]`, `Yeast_Extract_Peptone[1]`, and new `togo_m2491_mrssi_base[8]`. The literal source evidence supports generic peptone; it does not establish Bacto, animal origin, digest method or a supplier. Retarget only after the exact final generic owner and consumer are reviewed together.\n- Ten unresolved source-identity claims: `Fastidious_Anaerobe_Broth_With_Meat_Granules[1]`, `PY-cellobiose[0]`, `PY-fructose[0]`, `PY-glucose-rumen_Fluid[0]`, `PY-maltose[0]`, `PY-pectin[0]`, `PYEG[0]`, `PYG-002_Tween_80[0]`, `PYG[0]`, `PYG_Rumen_Fluid[0]`. The inherited edges depend on abbreviations or research interpretation. Recover the source identity, or independently review withdrawal of the unsupported resolving identifier to `UNMAPPED` while retaining the literal component and provenance. A hold note must not leave a now-misleading Bacto-resolving identifier in place.\n- Retain the source-specific `GYPS[2]` Bacto reference: its original publication p.1622 explicitly specifies Bacto-peptone (Difco). Do not globally replace this reference with generic peptone.\n- The current combined Marine Broth proposal already withdraws `Marine_Broth_2216[0]` to `UNMAPPED`; preserve its nominal-formula scope and existing product/lot limits.\n\nThe actual native counterfactual is important: changing generic Peptone alone produces zero component-partonomy errors, because the Bacto owner still represents `MICRO:0000178`. Structural green therefore cannot authorize these source referents. This follows MAPPING_SEMANTICS §6: the CURIE denotes the part identity, not a unique document.\n\nCompose overlapping corrections on one final payload: Fastidious also has a cooked-meat withdrawal; PY-glucose-rumen and PYG_Rumen also have rumen withdrawals under #1204. Preserve every preimage, quantity, source assertion and history; no global identifier replacement, owner merging, or approval transfer. The broader source/role/export holds remain.\n\nEvidence is pinned in `preflight/final-component-dependency-plan-v1/minimal-couplings-28.json` and its complete 435-claim replay. The explicit accounting cutoff is 2026-11-08T07:59:05Z; later accepted worker heads must be rebound and re-enumerated before application. #710 is retained as historical semantic-review context, not an open implementation tracker.\n\nThe sealed origin addendum verifies existing authentic child proposals for the three rumen consumers, the cooked-meat consumers, and the other represented source cases. Twelve peptone consumers lack a source proposal: five conditional generic retargets and seven ambiguous claims needing evidence or a reviewed identifier withdrawal. The coordinator selects the existing-constructor route: W05 may add authentic dependent `edit_existing_owner` proposals bound to each actual child path and before hash, causally linked to its real generic-peptone case. This causal linkage must not pretend that the child recipe was observed in the shard, and does not itself settle any scientific identity. Existing child origins must be composed rather than duplicated.\n\nA separate direct guarded curation phase is also natively supported, but is not being inserted into an already frozen campaign source/publication checkpoint. No owner changes have been applied. All twenty peptone dispositions and the three overlapping consumer repairs require exact final composition and independent review.\n\nDependency plan manifest SHA256 `95cfc48d9fd943d9fca75c09c787b9e83521bb052e9c4909b3ad984b7539956e` (98members); authentic-origin/route addendum manifest `6e0df3e4513973fbc63277e17e80f078c6c2d3518039d2e7a90e99113e1f7a29` (28members). Both were rehashed by the coordinator. The addendum explicitly bridges current W01 da45d5a5 UW and W06 1d62a408 PYGS payloads; these are mechanical origin bridges, not new whole-owner approvals.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719248666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}